 https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316553\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/SelectableProfileService.sys.mjs", "browser/components/shell/CustomIconManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/shell/test/unit/test_customIconManager.js"], "git_node": "94b2b2df775ccdc4952236e7b634c5c73e82ec98", "git_parents": ["6e1741bba57235f405e9aa6e1bd0ec592af37b23"], "node": "2d9592a4bd4f0159e88acd2837e3bddfe64dd4cd", "parents": ["625983383569df20c25eeeb80ba73e7792253ada"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785951062, "git_changesets": ["6e1741bba57235f405e9aa6e1bd0ec592af37b23", "94b2b2df775ccdc4952236e7b634c5c73e82ec98"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27855": {"changesets": [{"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050294 - Backport cubeb test_loopback.cpp fix to address perma-failures on Windows. a=diannaS\n\nThis is a test-only change. To fix a perma, caused by a change in CI image.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315968\n", "files": ["media/libcubeb/0005-fix-loopback-separate-streams-flakiness-windows.patch", "media/libcubeb/moz.yaml", "media/libcubeb/test/test_loopback.cpp"], "git_node": "13cfdd7203fc221a65093b5624aaac024b3d8fca", "git_parents": ["94b2b2df775ccdc4952236e7b634c5c73e82ec98"], "node": "c8aac531aff812297691de37f3bf3050be1bff79", "parents": ["2d9592a4bd4f0159e88acd2837e3bddfe64dd4cd"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785952203, "git_changesets": ["13cfdd7203fc221a65093b5624aaac024b3d8fca"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "27856": {"changesets": [{"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053608 - Additional validation of URL segments in nsStandardURL.  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312991\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316599\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp"], "git_node": "d4267a943335169e3eb06342681f51f99b0de671", "git_parents": ["13cfdd7203fc221a65093b5624aaac024b3d8fca"], "node": "31c070eccd82dfa180bf6be39f5c74f5f335b425", "parents": ["c8aac531aff812297691de37f3bf3050be1bff79"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785955077, "git_changesets": ["d4267a943335169e3eb06342681f51f99b0de671"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27857": {"changesets": [{"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058008 - Make `TSFTextStoreBase` retrieve TSF attr \u003c-\u003e index with checking its type  a=diannaS\n\n`TSFTextStoreBase` should consider the number of supported TSF\nattributes from `IsEditable()` result which indicates whether the\ninstance is `TSFEmptyTextStore` or `TSFTextStore`.\n\nThen, we can simplify the implementation of\n`TSFTextStoreBase::HandleRequestAttrs` and\n`TSFTextStoreBase::RetrieveRequestedAttrsInternal`.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314564\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315918\n", "files": ["widget/windows/TSFEmptyTextStore.cpp", "widget/windows/TSFTextStore.cpp", "widget/windows/TSFTextStoreBase.cpp", "widget/windows/TSFTextStoreBase.h", "widget/windows/TSFUtils.cpp", "widget/windows/TSFUtils.h"], "git_node": "c95087e7b42e85198251f52749f46ce08e7d33d6", "git_parents": ["d4267a943335169e3eb06342681f51f99b0de671"], "node": "b0b92f0bf8961de97ccbd7defe6c2b021b6c72c1", "parents": ["31c070eccd82dfa180bf6be39f5c74f5f335b425"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785955880, "git_changesets": ["c95087e7b42e85198251f52749f46ce08e7d33d6"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27858": {"changesets": [{"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053432 - Detect Android 17 Local Network Protection blocking TCP connections.  a=diannaS\n\nAndroid 17 enforces OS-level Local Network Protection: a TCP connect() to\na local-network address is silently blocked unless the app holds\nACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK/NEARBY_DEVICES (see\nhttps://developer.android.com/privacy-and-security/local-network-permission#strategy-by-use-case).\nFirefox's own LNA prompt only triggers after a successful connect, so this\nOS-level block never reaches that check and the load just fails with no\npath forward for the user.\n\nAdd an Android-only helper, netwerk/system/android/AndroidNetworkBlockedReason.{h,cpp},\nthat asks the OS directly via android_getnetworkblockedreason()\n(dlsym-resolved against libandroid.so, since the NDK doesn't declare it\nyet) whether a failed TCP connect in nsSocketTransport2.cpp was caused by\nthis block, failing it with a new, distinct\nNS_ERROR_OS_LOCAL_NETWORK_ACCESS_DENIED. A follow-up commit teaches\nnsDocShell and GeckoView to recognize it.\n\nQUIC/HTTP3 isn't detected separately: per Android's guidance (same link\nabove), a blocked UDP send just returns EPERM with no reliable way to\nattribute it specifically to this block, and necko already retries a\nfailed HTTP3 connection over TCP, which hits this same detection.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315953\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316470\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/moz.build", "netwerk/base/nsSocketTransport2.cpp", "netwerk/system/android/AndroidNetworkBlockedReason.cpp", "netwerk/system/android/AndroidNetworkBlockedReason.h", "netwerk/system/android/moz.build", "netwerk/test/gtest/TestSocketTransportService.cpp", "netwerk/test/gtest/moz.build", "xpcom/base/ErrorList.py"], "git_node": "9831ffa508306f6cc5969e100928e622a68057c8", "git_parents": ["c95087e7b42e85198251f52749f46ce08e7d33d6"], "node": "9d9c9e357d013d1d8227657a9000cc527be05aeb", "parents": ["b0b92f0bf8961de97ccbd7defe6c2b021b6c72c1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053432 - Surface OS-level Local Network Protection failures to GeckoView's onLoadError.  a=diannaS\n\nNS_ERROR_OS_LOCAL_NETWORK_ACCESS_DENIED was silently rewritten to NS_OK\nbefore reaching nsDocShell's error handling, so GeckoView's onLoadError\nnever fired for it.\n\nAdd it to FilterStatusForErrorPage's allowlist and to DisplayLoadError's\nclassification (temporarily grouped with NS_ERROR_NET_RESET, see TODO).\nBug 2057481 will intercept it in GeckoEngineSession.onLoadError()\n(android-components) to prompt for the nearby devices permission and\nreload on grant.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315954\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316471\n", "files": ["docshell/base/moz.build", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/base/test/gtest/TestFilterStatusForErrorPage.cpp", "docshell/base/test/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "90032ab2dbbfada9beca322ef71b7f93d6a4da51", "git_parents": ["9831ffa508306f6cc5969e100928e622a68057c8"], "node": "c88d8b20fc0788ee4a008dc6d87631aee3c61d02", "parents": ["9d9c9e357d013d1d8227657a9000cc527be05aeb"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785957298, "git_changesets": ["9831ffa508306f6cc5969e100928e622a68057c8", "90032ab2dbbfada9beca322ef71b7f93d6a4da51"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27859": {"changesets": [{"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060342 - Keep 3D-transformed text off the device glyph path  a=diannaS\n\nThe device glyph path has the shader map each glyph's device rect back to local\nspace with the full 4x4 inverse, z forced to 0. That only inverts how the\ntransform maps the glyphs' z=0 plane while the third row or the third column is\nentirely zero; when both carry terms the round trip displaces the quad and\noffsets its UV fraction, shaving a slice off every glyph. A perspective paired\nwith a translateZ hits this (bug 2052019 let it onto the path), and so does any\n3D rotation, which has been broken since bug 2044211.\n\nGate on is_2d_on_z_plane() instead of has_2d_plane_perspective(): the transform\nmust map that plane, and invert it, exactly as its 2D terms would. Requiring\nm44 == 1 as well keeps the fix CPU-side, with no shader change. A flat\nperspective and a bare translateZ each stay on the sharp device path; pairing\nthem, a 3D rotation, or a matrix3d with a constant w != 1 now rasterize in local\nspace.\n\nperspective-clip.png goes back to its pre-bug-2052019 rendering, since that\ntest's matrix pairs a perspective with a translateZ.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316117\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316371\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/text_run.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/util.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/3d-device-text.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/3d-device-text.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/perspective-clip.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/reftest.list"], "git_node": "7a8f6b060ae7482e21ac6aa2825781054df6aeb3", "git_parents": ["90032ab2dbbfada9beca322ef71b7f93d6a4da51"], "node": "6b600e678fa31d6e9ac63245f24655fdc2fa7111", "parents": ["c88d8b20fc0788ee4a008dc6d87631aee3c61d02"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785959508, "git_changesets": ["7a8f6b060ae7482e21ac6aa2825781054df6aeb3"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27860": {"changesets": [{"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053153 - Only check for high surrogates when intending to avoid split pair.  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314632\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316465\n", "files": ["parser/expat/13_high_surrogate_mask.patch", "parser/expat/expat/lib/xmltok.c", "parser/expat/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "fa9bdeb46b18693349d28e0ca328c85c7b33abfa", "git_parents": ["7a8f6b060ae7482e21ac6aa2825781054df6aeb3"], "node": "877258b367e2bfaa9cc20ba71d0e3e6c87043697", "parents": ["6b600e678fa31d6e9ac63245f24655fdc2fa7111"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785959627, "git_changesets": ["fa9bdeb46b18693349d28e0ca328c85c7b33abfa"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27861": {"changesets": [{"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgreg@gregstoll.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058002  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314740\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316042\n", "files": ["toolkit/xre/dllservices/mozglue/Authenticode.cpp"], "git_node": "50685c86da5ff71b1a2d4c837e02cdf9d138d03f", "git_parents": ["fa9bdeb46b18693349d28e0ca328c85c7b33abfa"], "node": "c599cec15e66920d44e2a1c8526bb0f06aed2b4f", "parents": ["877258b367e2bfaa9cc20ba71d0e3e6c87043697"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785959754, "git_changesets": ["50685c86da5ff71b1a2d4c837e02cdf9d138d03f"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27862": {"changesets": [{"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054116 - add a slack notification to desktop and android release mark-as-shipped. r=releng-reviewers,bhearsum a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313976\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/release-mark-as-shipped/kind.yml"], "git_node": "0937381970a4ae5bb48254dce5419adfa9138502", "git_parents": ["50685c86da5ff71b1a2d4c837e02cdf9d138d03f"], "node": "69811cbf13d3c1eb390229ee46d341292195ed22", "parents": ["c599cec15e66920d44e2a1c8526bb0f06aed2b4f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060000. r=gfx-reviewers,nical, a=dsmith\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315942\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLContextGL.cpp"], "git_node": "c3a0f25ab88320e1d522ef2400ad69b39fddc370", "git_parents": ["0937381970a4ae5bb48254dce5419adfa9138502"], "node": "627f4e1728de91654522052e124d319d71a9c164", "parents": ["69811cbf13d3c1eb390229ee46d341292195ed22"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785960612, "git_changesets": ["0937381970a4ae5bb48254dce5419adfa9138502", "c3a0f25ab88320e1d522ef2400ad69b39fddc370"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27863": {"changesets": [{"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059207 - Honor idExtension partition in the No-Vary-Search cache lookup,  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315290\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316478\n", "files": ["netwerk/cache2/CacheStorageService.cpp"], "git_node": "2b4a3fefd56de81752696e2372456494e3873dcc", "git_parents": ["c3a0f25ab88320e1d522ef2400ad69b39fddc370"], "node": "867020f62e8ba8568cf03389324deb6b81b733c4", "parents": ["627f4e1728de91654522052e124d319d71a9c164"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785961215, "git_changesets": ["2b4a3fefd56de81752696e2372456494e3873dcc"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27864": {"changesets": [{"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058611 - Clear form for element when insertion is aborted.  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315079\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316316\n", "files": ["parser/html/nsHtml5TreeOperation.cpp"], "git_node": "ea66776df55d772a4b42320a70204cbc3d3360c5", "git_parents": ["2b4a3fefd56de81752696e2372456494e3873dcc"], "node": "2b7e0c1747395825832cf64eb421d2708773de14", "parents": ["867020f62e8ba8568cf03389324deb6b81b733c4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785961243, "git_changesets": ["ea66776df55d772a4b42320a70204cbc3d3360c5"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27865": {"changesets": [{"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058622, validate selected options entries,  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314926\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316324\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLSelectElement.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/select-selectedOptions-nesting.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "01a69a92214fffbfb196b7de9d352ac180ebb961", "git_parents": ["ea66776df55d772a4b42320a70204cbc3d3360c5"], "node": "dbd17a3b3877e4eee1f31e7e29a54e6ae8c96c49", "parents": ["2b7e0c1747395825832cf64eb421d2708773de14"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785961280, "git_changesets": ["01a69a92214fffbfb196b7de9d352ac180ebb961"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27866": {"changesets": [{"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053579 - avoid DescendingSeqNumComp\u003cuint16_t\u003e as comparator in std::set.  a=diannaS\n\nThis is a combined cherry-pick of upstream libwebrtc bf6f744d19, 5ecea90550,\n6395da1ed7.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/bf6f744d19a84a7d0c3f5acbc844123a8197165a\n       Check RTP sequence number order when assembling H264 frame in PacketBuffer\n\n       PacketBuffer::buffer_ slots can be re-used by packets with with\n       different sequence numbers when their difference is multiple of\n       buffer_.size()\n\n       Non-H264 code path validates RTP sequence numbers continuity in\n       `PotentialNewFrame` helper, H264 code path missed such check as the new\n       test demonstrate.\n\n       Bug: chromium:537233963\n       Change-Id: I6af0f52bfcb3a4437450dffcece85bee7ce172cd\n       Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/490840\n       Reviewed-by: \u00c5sa Persson \u003casapersson@webrtc.org\u003e\n       Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n       Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48222}\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/5ecea90550816628fa124e7cf55f4cdbc5aa4a7e\n       In PacketBuffer use helper to find packet slot in the buffer\n\n       This is a preparation for using unwrapped int64_t instead of wrapped\n       uint16_t RTP sequence number in PacketBuffer. Using modular works when\n       sequence number is unsigned but produces incorrect result when signed\n       sequence number happens to be negative.\n\n       Bug: chromium:537233963\n       Change-Id: I515cb7441d052a2823eee4891bb4e17b254d602f\n       Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/491920\n       Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n       Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n       Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48231}\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/6395da1ed7da9f3a8d97475c4e8db722d9415e6f\n       Use unwrappred RTP sequence numbers in PacketBuffer\n\n       Thus avoid brittle DescendingSeqNumComp\u003cuint16_t\u003e as comparator in set.\n       Such comparator lacks some properties like transitivity making it\n       dangerous to use with the std::set\n\n       Bug: chromium:537233963\n       Change-Id: I400b423ab3f0d557219d459752e00d211fd97450\n       Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/491041\n       Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n       Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n       Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48232}\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316656\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/rtp_video_frame_assembler.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/packet_buffer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/packet_buffer.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/packet_buffer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/rtp_video_stream_receiver2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/rtp_video_stream_receiver2.h"], "git_node": "afa894aaad4c1dc7fa412e5d9cc2a423d7a6fceb", "git_parents": ["01a69a92214fffbfb196b7de9d352ac180ebb961"], "node": "81c2314df8d116ed1649f626b7fb98389746ee79", "parents": ["dbd17a3b3877e4eee1f31e7e29a54e6ae8c96c49"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785978977, "git_changesets": ["afa894aaad4c1dc7fa412e5d9cc2a423d7a6fceb"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27867": {"changesets": [{"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059825 - Use Cu.isInAutomation for enterprise policy test overrides.  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315723\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316610\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/backgroundtasks/tests/BackgroundTask_policies.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/backgroundtasks/tests/browser/browser_xpcom_graph_wait.js", "toolkit/components/enterprisepolicies/EnterprisePoliciesParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d45c38f4bf8df0fcbf7ca0ca010c62b4a76173d0", "git_parents": ["afa894aaad4c1dc7fa412e5d9cc2a423d7a6fceb"], "node": "99aa142233d3f0f1f45c4ce1bcf892afeb64ba7e", "parents": ["81c2314df8d116ed1649f626b7fb98389746ee79"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785979769, "git_changesets": ["d45c38f4bf8df0fcbf7ca0ca010c62b4a76173d0"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27868": {"changesets": [{"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054740 - Harden image transferable buffer size validation;  a=diannaS\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316442\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "gfx/2d/DataSurfaceHelpers.cpp"], "git_node": "3d295114897ce2aeab72b42cae0ef9057f964f9f", "git_parents": ["d45c38f4bf8df0fcbf7ca0ca010c62b4a76173d0"], "node": "c99774e07e7f926a6a78e6ba7573a6ae3762d221", "parents": ["99aa142233d3f0f1f45c4ce1bcf892afeb64ba7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060106.  a=diannaS\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316443\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "52f1c0a6b7559845c51f7f5f6e79da6e2498a93f", "git_parents": ["3d295114897ce2aeab72b42cae0ef9057f964f9f"], "node": "2f11db8186f496c7709c5dafc3d29613cc5f0975", "parents": ["c99774e07e7f926a6a78e6ba7573a6ae3762d221"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785981104, "git_changesets": ["3d295114897ce2aeab72b42cae0ef9057f964f9f", "52f1c0a6b75598