c3d4e8055abec5ac82 with DEVEDITION_154_0b8_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "1e27174ac0fb0981f3a017c47082fd5f26a065e3", "git_parents": ["cf42a094c7a3d01f042afaf070eb1655186afce5"], "node": "e9cce50c217f08c1f5ecf95366bc56a82c6f108e", "parents": ["0bdda58291a3636a3b200cbc762b1217c4485527"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786115957, "git_changesets": ["1e27174ac0fb0981f3a017c47082fd5f26a065e3"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "27891": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 71247cf02ab057bd214802c3d4e8055abec5ac82 with FIREFOX_154_0b8_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "d7e283982dc12f8a695cef561f6e56a5e3e4c1c7", "git_parents": ["1e27174ac0fb0981f3a017c47082fd5f26a065e3"], "node": "f511ce65e85abba015c719f4d7edcac1c77a73fe", "parents": ["e9cce50c217f08c1f5ecf95366bc56a82c6f108e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786117321, "git_changesets": ["d7e283982dc12f8a695cef561f6e56a5e3e4c1c7"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "27892": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057205 - (Beta version) Don't repeat a non-repeating gradient because of rounding.  a=diannaS\n\nManually rebased on top of the beta branch to resolve conflicts.\n\noptimize_radial_gradient shrinks a gradient's primitive rect to the bounding box\nof the interesting part of the ellipse and pushes the removed margins into\ntile_spacing. simplify_repeated_primitive then collapses that back into a single\ntile, but the tile size is stored as a ratio of the primitive rect while\ntile_spacing stays absolute, and the ratio is computed against the unsnapped rect\nand resolved against the snapped one at prepare time. The round-trip is therefore\nnot exact and could yield a stretch size a fraction of a pixel smaller than the\nprimitive rect, making prepare_repeatable_quad believe the primitive repeats.\n\nTwo fixes:\n\n - compute_stretch_ratio now reports exactly 1.0 on an axis where the tile\n   fuzzily covers the whole primitive rect, so a non-repeating primitive can't\n   be resurrected as a repeating one with a sub-pixel stride.\n\n - The CPU repetition loop now clips each tile to the primitive rect as well as\n   to the local clip rect. The last tile of a row or column always overhangs the\n   primitive rect and used to rely on the local clip rect bounding it, which is\n   not an invariant optimize_radial_gradient preserves. Without this the spurious\n   repetition rendered a complete, unclipped duplicate of the gradient.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314908\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317049\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/prim_geometry.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/radial-spurious-repeat-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/radial-spurious-repeat.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/reftest.list"], "git_node": "2f148989ebdfbfb93e649673e220c6f8afb5d311", "git_parents": ["140333b8dd949c7b84e70e98d86efdf01506e0e6"], "node": "7275f6e85cd3c057b87c723bffa2369df1cef407", "parents": ["0199ea631636941102539cabe2f848367fed0db9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786122154, "git_changesets": ["2f148989ebdfbfb93e649673e220c6f8afb5d311"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27893": {"changesets": [{"author": "Dave Townsend \u003cdtownsend@oxymoronical.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059430: Simplify writing new profile preferences.  a=diannaS\n\nThis also removes the additional write of DAU_GROUPID_PREF_NAME which will have already been read from the database.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315298\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317035\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/SelectableProfileService.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "4e604506a7e03419984e7a191b351736ad24c64b", "git_parents": ["2f148989ebdfbfb93e649673e220c6f8afb5d311"], "node": "f184a434047169f7a504db4c4bfa6c44f84ba8b0", "parents": ["7275f6e85cd3c057b87c723bffa2369df1cef407"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786122184, "git_changesets": ["4e604506a7e03419984e7a191b351736ad24c64b"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27894": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051882 - Part 1: Fix handling of budget expiry during main thread only marking  a=diannaS\n\nCurrently we don't take account of the fact that we may run out of budget doing\nmain-thread-only marking at the start of a marking slice and return Finished\nwhen we're not.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310035\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317020\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/GC.cpp", "js/src/gc/GCRuntime.h", "js/src/gc/Sweeping.cpp"], "git_node": "95281e195392879e9a0f87ceac72d7198318659f", "git_parents": ["4e604506a7e03419984e7a191b351736ad24c64b"], "node": "41ec0a5446ec152c346159ee4e8826b22b8f2864", "parents": ["f184a434047169f7a504db4c4bfa6c44f84ba8b0"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786122649, "git_changesets": ["95281e195392879e9a0f87ceac72d7198318659f"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27895": {"changesets": [{"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060357.  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316207\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316213\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/SharedRGBImage.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/SharedRGBImage.h"], "git_node": "f02a602ad8d6b71a1185c7d668d0d56ec7034363", "git_parents": ["95281e195392879e9a0f87ceac72d7198318659f"], "node": "19acfb38bdedd87805ac5b0538846bedf53fd427", "parents": ["41ec0a5446ec152c346159ee4e8826b22b8f2864"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786122781, "git_changesets": ["f02a602ad8d6b71a1185c7d668d0d56ec7034363"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27896": {"changesets": [{"author": "Vincent Hilla \u003cvhilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060799 - Harden against re-bindign an already-parented node.  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316497\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317002\n", "files": ["dom/base/CharacterData.cpp", "dom/base/Element.cpp", "dom/base/nsINode.cpp"], "git_node": "cd2aa600c728902b5869d1fd4081a81562b1c395", "git_parents": ["f02a602ad8d6b71a1185c7d668d0d56ec7034363"], "node": "6bff2d353aebf0f0b27ca3afd07cb51933a87bb0", "parents": ["19acfb38bdedd87805ac5b0538846bedf53fd427"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786122813, "git_changesets": ["cd2aa600c728902b5869d1fd4081a81562b1c395"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27897": {"changesets": [{"author": "yazan \u003cyalmacki@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056382 - Add a shortcut to per user start menu folder so taskbar icon can be modified.  a=diannaS\n\nThe taskbar falls back to using the icon of the shortcut (with a matching AUMID) located at the system-wide start menu path, when a matching shortcut doesn\u2019t exist at the user-level start menu. We cannot modify the icon at the system-wide shortcut so it stays the same.\n\nWhen pinned, a shortcut gets created at the user-level, which we can edit, and hence the problem doesn\u2019t exist there. The fix is to add a shortcut to the per user start menu directory. The shell prioritizes that shortcut\u2019s icon over the system-wide one when both are present, and we have the ability to modify it.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313551\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316939\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/config/browser-icon.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/SelectableProfileService.sys.mjs", "browser/components/shell/CustomIconManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/shell/StartupOSIntegration.sys.mjs", "browser/components/shell/test/unit/test_customIconManager.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2056382_browser_shortcut_description.py", "widget/nsIWinTaskbar.idl", "widget/windows/WinTaskbar.cpp"], "git_node": "882dcf80f550f5bef4a90fe50d71eef26faca339", "git_parents": ["cd2aa600c728902b5869d1fd4081a81562b1c395"], "node": "c2d5e5e6546fc25959b5a510c26738419d3e94d8", "parents": ["6bff2d353aebf0f0b27ca3afd07cb51933a87bb0"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786122847, "git_changesets": ["882dcf80f550f5bef4a90fe50d71eef26faca339"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27898": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059996 - (Beta version) Fix width/height inversion in QuadTileClassifier.  a=diannaS\n\nManually rebased on top of the beta branch to resolve conflicts.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316731\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317051\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/tiled-thin-quads-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/tiled-thin-quads.yaml"], "git_node": "77fb225476bc100510955b81fecd0688dc894455", "git_parents": ["882dcf80f550f5bef4a90fe50d71eef26faca339"], "node": "226d1385ac98a2376056d95c729c134aaca03ba3", "parents": ["c2d5e5e6546fc25959b5a510c26738419d3e94d8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786123182, "git_changesets": ["77fb225476bc100510955b81fecd0688dc894455"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27899": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056065 - Hold a strong ref to platform font entry.  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316012\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316491\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxTextRun.cpp"], "git_node": "362c7a58e1b0c60c9bf5a71aa934d6557032ffbb", "git_parents": ["77fb225476bc100510955b81fecd0688dc894455"], "node": "1ec7c0408e26d6fb3dd27b7ba785d3e894eb7e95", "parents": ["226d1385ac98a2376056d95c729c134aaca03ba3"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786123215, "git_changesets": ["362c7a58e1b0c60c9bf5a71aa934d6557032ffbb"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27900": {"changesets": [{"author": "Teodor Tanasoaia \u003cttanasoaia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059019.  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316234\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316999\n", "files": ["dom/webgpu/ExternalTexture.cpp", "gfx/gl/GLBlitHelperD3D.cpp", "gfx/layers/d3d11/GpuProcessD3D11TextureMap.cpp", "gfx/layers/d3d11/GpuProcessD3D11TextureMap.h"], "git_node": "57ca3d20a97275b7b903fab0e7d7eb8ecef5f063", "git_parents": ["362c7a58e1b0c60c9bf5a71aa934d6557032ffbb"], "node": "07bce05c0da9ab9aa44bd7cd845e5a0ebc0c9de4", "parents": ["1ec7c0408e26d6fb3dd27b7ba785d3e894eb7e95"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786124076, "git_changesets": ["57ca3d20a97275b7b903fab0e7d7eb8ecef5f063"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27901": {"changesets": [{"author": "Simon Chopin \u003cschopin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058991 - Make Windows InstallTime crash annotation stable, take 2  a=diannaS\n\nDue to some slightly misguided suggestion from yours truly, the first\nattempt at stabilisation ended up still reading an actual pointer value\nrather than the data pointed to.\n\nIn addition to fixing the code, this patch separates it into discrete\nfunctions for testability, adds tests, and guards against some possible\nweirdness, e.g. if in the future the SID ends up not being at the end of\nthe payload.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314977\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317004\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/crash_helper_common/src/appinfo/windows.rs", "toolkit/library/rust/moz.build"], "git_node": "142cc3e2c38739501ee79749ce0175973845c031", "git_parents": ["57ca3d20a97275b7b903fab0e7d7eb8ecef5f063"], "node": "2005243e39d08ff7474e8272d67e3941c223e484", "parents": ["07bce05c0da9ab9aa44bd7cd845e5a0ebc0c9de4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786130691, "git_changesets": ["142cc3e2c38739501ee79749ce0175973845c031"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27902": {"changesets": [{"author": "chloezhouny \u003cchloezhouny@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051361 - Add a chat history entry point to the Smart Window assistant.  a=diannaS\n\nSidebar: a \"...\" button next to New chat opens a menu that navigates in place from a main view - Chat history and Smart Window settings - to a chat history subview listing recent chats plus a shortcut to all chats.\n\nFullpage: a labeled top-actions row - New chat, Chat history, and More. Chat history opens a dropdown of recent chats and a \"View all chats\" shortcut; More holds Smart Window settings.\n\nRecent chats are tab-specific: selecting one switches to its tab if open, otherwise reopens it in a new tab. \"View all chats\" opens the Chats section of Firefox View.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313089\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317133\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-history-menu/smartwindow-history-menu.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-history-menu/smartwindow-history-menu.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-history-menu/smartwindow-history-menu.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindowMenu.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindowUI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ChatMessage.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ChatSql.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ChatStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_history_menu.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_new_chat_button.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/aiWindow.ftl"], "git_node": "e3e973968bd3196ba5fb9b3b07c090ee32b09855", "git_parents": ["142cc3e2c38739501ee79749ce0175973845c031"], "node": "b216fafb85a53fed259248f930d398371671a80f", "parents": ["2005243e39d08ff7474e8272d67e3941c223e484"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786131889, "git_changesets": ["e3e973968bd3196ba5fb9b3b07c090ee32b09855"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27903": {"changesets": [{"author": "Maile Lucks \u003cmaile.lucks@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056384 - Chatbot SW Promo -  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313128\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317124\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/ASRouterAdmin/ASRouterAdmin.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/schemas/MessagingExperiment.schema.json", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/schemas/make-schemas.py", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/templates/OnboardingMessage/SidebarChatBotPromo.schema.json", "browser/components/asrouter/content/asrouter-admin.bundle.js", "browser/components/asrouter/docs/index.md", "browser/components/asrouter/docs/messaging-surfaces.md", "browser/components/asrouter/docs/sidebar-chatbot-promo.md", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/ASRouter.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/ASRouterParentProcessMessageHandler.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/ASRouterTelemetry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/ActorConstants.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/PanelTestProvider.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/SidebarChatBotPromo.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/moz.build", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/xpcshell/head.js", "browser/components/genai/chat.css", "browser/components/genai/chat.html", "browser/components/genai/content/chatbot-promo.css", "browser/components/genai/content/chatbot-promo.mjs", "browser/components/genai/content/chatbot-promo.stories.mjs", "browser/components/genai/jar.mn", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_promo.js", "browser/components/messagepreview/actors/AboutMessagePreviewParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/storybook/.storybook/main.js"], "git_node": "9706ef0d095d16e6ca09df1f10b91baae56ddeb0", "git_parents": ["e3e973968bd3196ba5fb9b3b07c090ee32b09855"], "node": "9c0c0e739a11c0af0d143b2053608798e2582d51", "parents": ["b216fafb85a53fed259248f930d398371671a80f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786131916, "git_changesets": ["9706ef0d095d16e6ca09df1f10b91baae56ddeb0"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27904": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-beta repo-update HSTS HPKP -  a=diannaS\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317147\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc"], "git_node": "caeeec47abfb92c5adce0957396b006c5ea013ef", "git_parents": ["9706ef0d095d16e6ca09df1f10b91baae56ddeb0"], "node": "af9b0262cb366b3f29c0bdf02ab8fd6d84832c74", "parents": ["9c0c0e739a11c0af0d143b2053608798e2582d51"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786135095, "git_changesets": ["caeeec47abfb92c5adce0957396b006c5ea013ef"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27905": {"changesets": [{"author": "Kelly Cochrane \u003ckcochrane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061026 - Fix for overflowing summary headers for cards in the History sidebar panel  a=diannaS\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316803\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316836\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/sidebar.css"], "git_node": "024b4bd2bf6c62e07155473b4adad83e4398c5b8", "git_parents": ["caeeec47abfb92c5adce0957396b006c5ea013ef"], "node": "7d093bf720d7817141c7453b8a3a91a0c49ccf60", "parents": ["af9b0262cb366b3f29c0bdf02ab8fd6d84832c74"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786135697, "git_changesets": ["024b4bd2bf6c62e07155473b4adad83e4398c5b8"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27906": {"changesets": [{"author": "Vasish Baungally \u003cvbaungally@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060260 - Add agglomerative clustering algorithm for Auto Tab Grouping.  a=diannaS\n\nThis patch  switches the KMeans clustering algorithm used for Auto Tab Grouping to\nAgglomerative clustering. The latter is more performant and has better metrics on our\ngolden dataset. It is also deterministic.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316350\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316943\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/SmartTabGrouping.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/smarttabgrouping/browser_tab_grouping.js", "toolkit/components/ml/content/ClusterAlgos.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_smart_tab_clustering_perf.js"], "git_node": "59063d42b5aa9c497c8d0e840539c658f8ac937d", "git_parents": ["024b4bd2bf6c62e07155473b4adad83e4398c5b8"], "node": "c186816f39d4dc8829566a8fa4f4447a167fd805", "parents": ["7d093bf720d7817141c7453b8a3a91a0c49ccf60"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786135844, "git_changesets": ["59063d42b5aa9c497c8d0e840539c658f8ac937d"], "user": "dsmith@mozilla.com"}, "27907": {"changesets": [{"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058205 - Show real tab favicons in the Auto Tab Grouping panel  a=diannaS DONTBUILD\n\nAuto Tab Grouping / 'Organize Tabs'\n\nFigma: https://www.figma.com/design/75Z1LtkCEUJWCxoY2KyNHv/Smart-Window-Q